findings.suggestion:
Use `issubclass(get_user_model(), field.model)` instead of `field.model == get_user_model()`. This correctly handles both the direct case (where `field.model` IS the user model, since `issubclass(X, X)` is True) and the MTI case (where the user model is a subclass of the model where the field is defined), while still excluding unrelated models that merely inherit from `AbstractBaseUser`:

```python
if field.name == "password" and issubclass(get_user_model(), field.model):
    return render_password_as_hash(value)
```
